   "subject": "Is it possible to plot the prior and likelihood of a given brms model?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I know there are various ways to plot the posterior distribution. But I can&#39;t seem to find anything about plotting the prior and likelihood distributions?</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "McxPkliBAQAJ",
   "from": "Paul Buerkner",
   "author": "6e3dd74b422c061b",
   "date": "2018-03-11T07:54:22Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] Is it possible to plot the prior and likelihood of a given brms model?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div>You can plot prior distributions for instance via <br><br></div>fit &lt;- brm(..., sample_prior = TRUE)<br></div>plot(hypothesis(fit, ...))<br><br></div>You cannot plot the likelihood, but you can plot the posterior-predictive distribution, which is way more informative, via pp_check(fit, ...)<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
